# Environment variables shared by bash and zsh.
#
# Sourced from bash/profile and zsh/zprofile, i.e. login shells only. Exports
# are inherited by every child process, so setting them once per session is
# enough. Keep this file POSIX-ish: it is read by both shells.
#
# Interactive-only settings (aliases, functions, prompt, fzf) belong in
# shell/aliases, which the rc files source for every interactive shell.

# Emit build/compile_commands.json on every configure so clangd can resolve
# includes and index the whole project; without it clangd parses each file with
# bare default flags and cross-file navigation does not work. CMake 3.17+ reads
# this as the default for the CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS variable. Note that
# clangd only auto-discovers the database in the project root or a `build/`
# subdirectory — other build dir names need a .clangd with CompilationDatabase.
command -v cmake >/dev/null 2>&1 && export CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS=ON
